Lab 1: Check your hostname

Run:

hostname

Example output:

bilal-ahmed-VMware-Virtual-Platform

This is your computer's name.

Now run:

hostname -I

Example:

192.168.1.105

This shows your VM's IP address.

=> Remember
hostname = Computer name
hostname -I = Computer IP address

Lab 2: Check DNS configuration

Run:

cat /etc/resolv.conf

You may see:

nameserver 127.0.0.53

or another IP.

Understand the output

If you see:

nameserver 127.0.0.53

It means:

Ubuntu is using a local DNS listener.

If you see:

nameserver 8.8.8.8

It means:

Ubuntu is configured to ask Google's DNS server.

Lab 3: Resolve a website name

Run:

getent hosts google.com

Example output:

142.250.x.x google.com
What happened?

You asked:

"What is the IP address of google.com?"

Ubuntu answered.

That is DNS resolution.

Remember this command
getent hosts google.com

Means:

Find the IP address of google.com.

